{"_id":"68a736428ec3d8323af203e4","nodeId":"EtVwQ4lnWi3IIFHGb2Qib","roadmapSlug":"typescript","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:45.916Z","description":"# Namespaces\n\nNamespaces in TypeScript are a way to organize code into logical groups, preventing naming collisions and improving code maintainability. They create a named container where you can define variables, functions, classes, and interfaces. By using namespaces, you can encapsulate related functionality under a specific name, making your code more structured and easier to understand.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Overview of Namespaces","url":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/namespaces.html","_id":"69a965b0ff22997353243963"},{"type":"official","title":"Namespaces and Modules","url":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/namespaces-and-modules.html","_id":"69a965b0ff22997353243964"},{"type":"official","title":"TypeScript - Using Namespaces","url":"https://typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/namespaces-and-modules.html#using-namespaces","_id":"69a965b0ff22997353243965"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-05T11:14:56.641Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04dcfb5fcb94d041649f","title":"Scrimba - Learn TypeScript","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"https://v2.scrimba.com/learn-typescript-c03c?via=roadmap"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/typescript/content/EtVwQ4lnWi3IIFHGb2Qib.md"}